fastgrib/tables/eccodes.py (GRIB2 parameter concepts: shortName, name, units) and
the typeOfLevel names in fastgrib/tables/levels.py are generated from the
definitions of ECMWF ecCodes 2.50.0 (tools/tables/make_eccodes.py,
tools/tables/make_levels.py), under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see
LICENSE-ecCodes). ecCodes' NOTICE reads, in part:

    ECMWF ecCodes
    (C) Copyright 2005- ECMWF.

    This product includes software developed at ECMWF (http://www.ecmwf.int).

    Parts of the definitions provided by WMO (https://public.wmo.int/en)

The level wording in fastgrib/tables/levels.py is taken from wgrib2's Level.c
(Wesley Ebisuzaki, NOAA/NCEP), which is in the public domain. NCEP's
parameter names in fastgrib/tables/params.py are from NCEP's GRIB2 documentation,
a US government work (public domain).

fastgrib/tables/params1_ecmwf.py (ECMWF's GRIB1 parameters and the GRIB2 numbers,
levels and statistics they read as) is generated from the GRIB1 and GRIB2
definitions of ECMWF ecCodes 2.50.0 (tools/tables/make_params1_ecmwf.py), under
the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-ecCodes).

fastgrib/tables/params1.py (NCEP's GRIB1 parameter tables: ON388 Table 2 and its
local tables 128-141) is generated from NCEP's ON388 documentation, a US
government work (public domain).

fastgrib/tables/chem.py (GRIB2 code table 4.230, WMO Common Code Table C-14) is
generated from WMO's own tables (github.com/wmo-im/CCT, C14.csv;
tools/tables/make_chem.py), under the MIT License (see LICENSE-WMO-CCT).

fastgrib/tables/ncep_grids.py (NCEP's predefined GRIB1 grids) is generated from
NCEP's ON388 Table B page (tools/tables/make_ncep_grids.py), a US government work
(public domain). WMO's international exchange grids in fastgrib/_grib1.py
follow WMO's Manual on Codes (FM 92 GRIB edition 1, Table B).

fastgrib/_jpeg2000.py (the JPEG2000 codec) is written from ITU-T T.800 |
ISO/IEC 15444-1 and checked against OpenJPEG (BSD 2-Clause License), whose
library tools/testdata/opj_tool.c links to make the test codestreams; no
OpenJPEG code is included. Staggered grids are placed as WMO's Manual on
Codes defines the scanning flags and as wgrib2 places them (its stagger.c is
in the public domain; no code taken); NCEP's rotated E- and B-grids as NCEP's
GRIB documentation (ON388, the GRIB2 templates 3.32768 and 3.32769) describes
them, a US government work (public domain).
